<title>ESTONIA: RAKVERE SAYS LATVIAN LONG-TERM.</title>
<headline>RAKVERE SAYS LATVIAN LONG-TERM.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rakvere meat factory said on Friday that its acquisition of a 67 percent stake in Riga meat factory will not raise its 1997 profit forecast, saying that it is a long-term investment.</p>
<p>&quot;It will not shake our 1997 estimate of 670 million kroons in turnover and 12 million kroons in profit, but its impact in the future will increase these figures,&quot; Teet Soorm, the company's finance director, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Rakvere meat factory will finance the deal from the its long-term credit and partly from its equity, Soorm said.</p>
<p>Rakvere has paid for part of the deal and the rest is to be paid according to schedule, he added.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
